From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:30:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] main: create the default GVfs and proxy resolver before any thread

geoclue sometimes never takes its bus name at boot, so systemd kills it
after the 45 s start timeout ("geoclue.service: start operation timed
out") and GNOME's colour, date/time and shell clients time out too. A
core taken at the timeout shows a deadlock in GIO:

- the main thread, in on_bus_acquired() -> gclue_locator_new() ->
  g_file_new_for_path(), is inside the default-VFS once-init and blocks
  on GIO's module lock in _g_io_module_get_default();
- a GNetworkMonitor can_reach worker holds that lock while
  g_proxy_resolver_get_default() constructs the libproxy resolver,
  whose sysconfig plugin calls g_file_new_for_path() and waits for the
  default-VFS once-init the main thread is in.

Create both singletons at the top of main(), before any other thread
exists, so neither initialisation can run while the other waits.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
--- a/src/gclue-main.c	2026-11-13 21:25:47
+++ b/src/gclue-main.c	2026-11-13 21:26:18
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include <config.h>
 
 #include <glib.h>
+#include <gio/gio.h>
 #include <locale.h>
 #include <glib/gi18n.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
@@ -190,6 +191,18 @@
         if (nmea_socket != NULL)
                 gclue_config_set_nmea_socket (config, nmea_socket);
 
+        /* Set up GIO's default VFS and proxy resolver now, while this is
+         * the only thread. Both are created by _g_io_module_get_default(),
+         * which holds GIO's module lock while it constructs the
+         * implementation, and the libproxy resolver creates a GFile (so it
+         * needs the default VFS) while it is constructed. Left to first use,
+         * a GNetworkMonitor worker thread creating the resolver and this
+         * thread creating the VFS (gclue_locator_new() -> g_file_new_for_path())
+         * can each wait for the other forever, and the service never takes
+         * its bus name. */
+        g_vfs_get_default ();
+        g_proxy_resolver_get_default ();
+
         owner_id = g_bus_own_name (G_BUS_TYPE_SYSTEM,
                                    BUS_NAME,
                                    G_BUS_NAME_OWNER_FLAGS_NONE,
